      "message": "serve: remember how fast each model really runs; scan the folder atomically\n\nEvery reply carries llama-server's timings; metalfit keeps the last 30 per\nmodel and Mac and shows the medians (writing at short and long context, reading\nprompts) in `metalfit list`, /api/status and the menu bar. Measured, not\npredicted: on a 32 GB M1 Max (24-core GPU) Qwen3.6-35B-A3B follows the bytes it\nreads per token, but Qwen3.8-27B ran GPU-bound at 99 % busy, about 90 GB/s, and\nthe same model wrote 7.1 to 10.7 tok/s depending on what ran before.\n\nThe model list was stale while a rescan ran: the first caller stored the new\nfolder signature before scanning, so requests arriving meanwhile got the old\nlist. Scans now hold a lock and keep the signature only when done, and reuse\nheaders of files that did not change.\n\nVersion 0.3.0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
