      },
      "message": "release: a self-contained MetalfitBar.app and a one-line install\n\nrelease/build.sh puts Python 3.12 (uv's python-build-standalone, without tests,\nTk and headers), metalfit and a Metal llama-server into the app, compiles every\n.pyc up front (a __pycache__ written later would break the signature), signs ad\nhoc and zips it: 75 MB app, 31 MB zip. release/install.sh downloads it with curl,\nchecks SHA256SUMS, replaces an older copy after stopping its server, and starts\nit. Installed this way on a 32 GB M1 Max, the bundled server wrote 47.7 tok/s\nwith Qwen3.6-35B-A3B UD-Q3_K_XL against 48.1 measured before.\n\nThe app is built for macOS 13 and llama-server for 14 (both were 26.0 before).\nVersion 0.2.0; `python -m metalfit` runs the CLI.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
