      "message": "serve: preload a model, and stop defaulting to the largest context\n\nTwo reasons a chat app got no answer, both of them this tool's fault:\n\n- best_ctx took the largest context that fits, so a 21 GB model loaded\n  at -c 131072 and took 69 s to do it.  A big KV cache makes loading\n  slow; it does not make answers better.  The default is now 32768 and\n  --ctx raises it deliberately.\n- nothing was loaded until the first message arrived, so that message\n  waited out the whole load.  --preload NAME loads and warms a model at\n  startup instead.\n\nMeasured after, five chat requests in a row through the proxy: worst\nfirst token 0.7 s, 55-65 tok/s.  Before: 69 s before anything came back,\nwhich Open WebUI gave up on.\n\nrun.sh now preloads, uses -c 32768 and keeps the model (KEEP_ALIVE=0),\nbecause a model that unloads itself makes the next message wait a minute\nagain.  That holds 24.4 GiB; stop metalfit when the memory is needed -\npredictable beats clever.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
