      "committer": {
        "name": "shruxx",
        "email": "24369531+shruxx@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-10-06T13:18:31Z"
      },
      "message": "proxy: --no-thinking, for reasoning models that never stop reasoning\n\nA reasoning model quantized hard can deliberate without ever answering.\nKolibri-1 at 2.7 bits (IQ2_M, imatrix) was asked for one PowerShell\nscript: 12000 tokens and 194 s of thinking, no code.  With the chat\ntemplate's enable_thinking off it wrote the same script in 1641 tokens\nand 25 s.  The 2.96-bit and 2.5-bit variants did the same on a twelve-row\narithmetic question - sum correct inside the trace, no answer out.\n\nSo the proxy can set chat_template_kwargs.enable_thinking=false on\nforwarded chat requests, which a chat app cannot do for itself.  A\nclient that sets chat_template_kwargs itself is left alone.\n\nMeasured through the proxy afterwards, with nothing special in the\nrequest: 1466 tokens, 23 s, an actual script.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
